
"smart_sources:2026-05-04 - The plight of the pinecone cowboy.md": {"path":"2026-05-04 - The plight of the pinecone cowboy.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"ly2akg","at":1785795032679},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783542856397,"size":33993,"at":1785795032775,"hash":"ly2akg"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,186]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Dillon Osleger","target":"Dillon Osleger","line":5},{"title":"These 50- to 70-year-old conifers were among the trees burned in the 2020 Castle Fire in California’s Giant Sequoia National Monument.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_3.jpg?w=2400&quality=100&ssl=1","line":24,"embedded":true},{"title":"Cruz McLean makes his way to the top of a giant sequoia to collect the tree’s best cones in Sequoia National Park, California.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_1-scaled.jpg?resize=2000%2C3065&quality=100&ssl=1","line":36,"embedded":true},{"title":"A Civilian Conservation Corps enrollee plants trees in 1933 as part of the Corps’ reforestation program. ","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_10.jpg?w=2000&quality=100&ssl=1","line":46,"embedded":true},{"title":"2022 congressional report","target":"https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R45688","line":54},{"title":"2015 Forest Service report","target":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/sites/default/files/2015-Fire-Budget-Report.pdf","line":54},{"title":"2026 budget","target":"https://www.usaspending.gov/federal_account/012-8046","line":58},{"title":"Just outside Sequoia National Park, California, reforestation workers Ruby and Stella Beauchamp carry crossbows used to hoist climbing ropes up and over tree branches.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_9.jpg?w=2400&quality=100&ssl=1","line":60,"embedded":true},{"title":"Stella Beauchamp holds a giant sequoia cone.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_12-scaled.jpg?resize=2000%2C3000&quality=100&ssl=1","line":70,"embedded":true},{"title":"*Forests*","target":"https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4907/12/12/1720","line":74},{"title":".","target":"https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4907/12/12/1720","line":74},{"title":"Robert Beauchamp, owner of Sierra Cone, one of the largest cone collection contractors in the West, reaches for a red fir cone outside of Dorrington, California.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_8.jpg?w=2400&quality=100&ssl=1","line":82,"embedded":true},{"title":"research says","target":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0378112723001822","line":88},{"title":"Forest Service research","target":"https://research.fs.usda.gov/treesearch/62002","line":92},{"title":"Red fir cones are prepared for transportation by Sierra Cone.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_6.jpg?w=2400&quality=100&ssl=1","line":108,"embedded":true},{"title":"Moonlight just outside Sequoia National Park, near the Alder Creek Grove.","target":"https://i0.wp.com/www.hcn.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pinecone-cowboys-58-05_11.jpg?w=2400&quality=100&ssl=1","line":124,"embedded":true},{"title":"*letter to the editor*","target":"https://www.hcn.org/feedback/contact-us","line":132},{"title":"*letters to the editor policy*","target":"https://www.hcn.org/policies/lte","line":132},{"title":"*editor@hcn.org*","target":"mailto:editor@hcn.org","line":132}],"metadata":{"title":"The plight of the pinecone cowboy","source":"https://www.hcn.org/issues/58-5/the-plight-of-the-pine-cone-cowboy/?emci=1f8d571c-9b49-f111-8ef2-000d3a14b640&emdi=730e2646-0c4a-f111-8ef2-000d3a14b640&ceid=110103","author":["[[Dillon Osleger]]"],"published":"2026-05-04","created":"2026-07-08","description":"As specialized forestry staff at the USFS vanish and pinecone cowboys—the highly skilled contractors sent out in the field to collect cones—face a collapsing industry, entire ecosystems are transforming in the West."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},